 "notes": "The arXiv paper (v2) reports dataset averages only (Table 1). Per-scene numbers exist only in the official repository results/*.csv, produced 2024-09-16 by decompressing the released ECCV models and rendering/measuring with the original 3DGS code; README states this fixes the earlier metric computation (quantization/compression loss now included, Dr Johnson moved to DeepBlending). Those CSV numbers are the decoded-model reference used here (the v2 Table-1 PSNRs are higher, e.g. Mip-NeRF360 27.64 vs CSV 27.08, while sizes agree: 40.3 MB vs CSV mean 40.28 MB). size_mb = 'Size [Bytes]' / 1e6, where Size = sum of all files in the compressed directory (*.jxl + compression_info.csv + compression_config.yml; decompress.py get_size_of_files_in_dir). baseline_3dgs = 3DGS row of the paper's Table 1 (authors' retrained 3DGS; average only; no per-scene baseline is published)."
